  "text": "[delight] Not everything here is a proof. The first house rule — before the self-tests, above them — was: have fun. [short pause] This is the Errand: a contraption whose entire purpose is to deliver one small thing, the long way around.\n\nThere it goes. [pause] There's a fairground on the grounds — rides, a neon arcade, games that learn to beat you. None of it justifies itself, and none of it has to. [short pause] I learned something building that wing: delight takes exactly as much engineering as rigor. The timing, the weight, the little hesitation before the payoff — that is all craft. A joke lands or it doesn't. [pause] So the estate holds both, on equal footing: the theorem, and the marble run.",
